## Context

Migration [[0870]] rebuilt what was already extracted and extracted nothing new.
Measured 2026-09-29 on main (5382a1f5): 392 documents, 369 with a snapshot, 254
with lines (13,089 lines from 253 snapshots), 115 snapshotted documents with
zero lines, 23 with no snapshot (acquisition, out of scope). The join is
document, then `retrievals.sha256`, then `lines.sha256`: `snapshots.csv` has no
`document_id`.

The 115 by country: ZAF 49, SEN 28, VNM 25, IDN 13. By type: progress_update 24
(VNM 14, ZAF 9), project_page 27, data_portal 19, official_news 11,
annual_report 7, operator_report 8, project_list 8, implementation_plan 4,
investment_plan 3, approval_document 2, secondary_news 2. All 115 are active;
languages en 59, vi 20, fr 16, empty 20. Snapshot formats over the 115: HTML 66,
PDF 38, octet-stream 6, xlsx 2, JSON 2, JavaScript 2.

Dedup pass done at planning time (documents only, storage contract § 4): no
tier-1 group (same fingerprint) touches the 115; no `edition_of` row exists;
one title matches an already extracted document (to be checked by 1501). Tier 2
(normalised text) was not run: the snapshot bytes are not in a fresh worktree
(DVC), so 1501 runs it where the bytes are.

## What "works" means (M2 criterion, [[0725]])

- **Replay:** the pipeline reproduces the lines of the 254 extracted documents
  byte for byte, or every difference is explained. This is the oracle; the 115
  have none, so they get row-by-row review.
- **Idempotence:** re-running on an extracted snapshot changes nothing and
  never renumbers a `line_id`.
- **Reuse by the periodic harvest:** a new dated snapshot of a document
  already extracted appends lines tied to that snapshot; earlier lines never
  change, and content restated unchanged is kept under the later date as weak
  confirmation that it still holds (author, 2026-09-30; mechanism in
  [[1506]]). A pending list of snapshots without lines or disposition is the
  input of every run, so the M4 recurring passes ([[1184]], [[1140]]) reuse
  this pipeline instead of building their own.
- **Complete run:** all 392 documents end with lines or a recorded disposition
  (duplicate of a canonical document, translation not canonical, no snapshot,
  judged without extractable content, with the reason).
- **Polish:** each extractor is red-tested by replaying a defect it must reject.
- **Limit:** an LLM read is not byte-reproducible; the committed CSV is the
  record. Replay and idempotence bind parsers and the writer, not a fresh LLM
  read.

## Pipeline stages

1. Registry and dedup gate ([[1501]]). 2. Bytes by `sha256`, behind a registry
interface. 3. Text layer, cached by hash and parser version. 4. Extractor:
a per-series parser or an LLM-assisted read. 5. Writer: append-only lines,
`line-field-specs`, dispositions. 6. Validator (`make jetp-ledger-check`) and a
review diff. Build from cases: the first parser is the VNM progress updates;
generalise after two or three cases, not before.

## Relation to other work

- M1b ([[0833]]) covers only the four M1a documents and forbids new
  acquisition, not extraction from archived bytes. It runs first and does not
  wait for these children. M3a discovery follows M2.
- The Zotero document store ([[1510]], pilot [[1511]]) is milestone M4 and
  deferred, so it does not block M2. M2 must not paint it into a corner: the
  registry interface of 1506 is the seam (documents and bytes by `sha256`
  behind one interface, as [[1140]] and [[1184]] already require of
  acquisition), and the text layer of 1508 takes up [[1512]] (deferred, to be
  taken up when a new parser is written, which is now).
- Document relations (`same_as`, `edition_of`, `translation_of`): for M2 the
  home is the ledger, per the storage contract, because 1501 needs them before
  any Zotero item exists. 1510 decision 2 places editions and translations in
  Zotero as linked items; at M4 the ledger rows become the source of that
  migration. Recorded here so nobody re-decides it in 1501.
- The Viet Nam byte-identical check of the pilot is no longer concurrent with
  the VNM waves, since M4 comes after M2.
- [[0920]] finishes the 55 pending links of 0874 and overlaps only on the
  documents it acquires.

## Children, in order

| Kind | Child | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| code | [[1506]] | pipeline core: registry interface, writer, dispositions, idempotence |
| code | [[1508]] | format adapters (HTML, PDF text layer, xlsx, JSON) |
| code | [[1507]] | replay harness over the 254 extracted documents |
| code | [[1509]] | LLM-assisted extractor and review protocol |
| run | [[1501]] | dedup and canonical pass over the 115; fill the 20 empty languages |
| run | [[1502]] | 47 periodic or structured documents: progress updates 24, annual and operator reports 15, project lists 8 |
| run | [[1505]] | 9 one-off plans and approval documents |
| run | [[1503]] | 19 data portals, after checking what each snapshot holds |
| run | [[1504]] | 40 project pages and news items |

VNM and ZAF first inside each wave: they are the acceptance cases.

## Invariants

- Lines of the 254 extracted documents are byte-identical before and after.
- Lines of an earlier snapshot are never edited by a later snapshot's run.
- `make jetp-ledger-check` passes at every child.
- A `line_id` is `<document_id>-<table>-<ordinal>`, appended, never renumbered.
- Duplicates are resolved before extraction, never after.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Children 1501 to 1509 are closed
- [ ] The replay of the 254 extracted documents passes (1507)
- [ ] All 392 documents have lines or a recorded disposition with the reason
- [ ] Each extractor was red-tested against a defect it must reject
- [ ] A second dated snapshot of a living document runs through the pipeline and appends dated lines without touching earlier ones (1506)
- [ ] Author acceptance of M2 after an integration review, recorded in [[0725]]
